<code>assert this.get(0).equals(item);</code>

However, based on the comment, it seems there might be a misunderstanding. The comment states "the added element is stored at the first position," which would imply that the element is added at index 0, making the stack LIFO behavior incorrect. Given the typical LIFO behavior of a stack, the element should be added at the top of the stack, which would be the last position, not the first. Therefore, the correct assertion should check if the element is at the last position:

<code>assert this.get(this.size() - 1).equals(item);</code>
--------------------
<code>assert this.get(0).equals(item);</code>
--------------------
